  "worked_solution": "The border-line is a vertical line passing through the point $(-4,0).$ Therefore, the line has the equation $x=-4.$\n\nNow, we need to decide which inequality symbol to use. Since the line is dashed, we will use a strict inequality. Since the shaded region is to the *right* of the line, the inequality refers to the $x$-values that are *greater than* those on the line $x=-4.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\nx>-4.\n$$",
